  "question": {
    "text": "A <math><mn>20</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>H</mtext></math> inductor coil is connected to a <math><mn>10</mn></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;resistance in series as shown in figure. The time at which rate of dissipation of energy&nbsp;(Joule&#39;s heat)&nbsp;across resistance is equal to the rate at which magnetic energy is stored in the inductor, is:<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/36cb4009-f746-4169-87cb-d4cdb6e75f7c-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 180px;\" />",
